        <head>VOLUNTEER PRIZE MEETING.</head>
        <p>VOLUNTEER PRIZE MEETING.</p>
        <p>The Results.</p>
        <p>-- The annual prize meeting in connection with the local Volunteer Battalion took place at the 'Appleton Range on Saturday and Monday. The men had to fire at a 3-inch bull, and in case of a competitor shooting twice the scores were added together and divided by two. Appended are the names and scores of the prize-winners : SERGEANTS' COMPETITION. 1. Sergeant-Drummer J. W. Plinston 2. Colour-Sergeant T. Ashworth 3. Sergeant E. Howard irccacolooßTrrpTi:oooßraraiaAdli LyTpas T. r: dia%cvloatlTtPar Taylor 4. Sergeant J. Lloyd 5. Sergeant J. L. Scott lorTrioN. 20 7. Quartermaster-Sergeant ,L NVillcock 21 19 3. Lance-Corporal T. Sumner l9 4. Corporal T. Daintith l9 5. Lance-Corporal J. Illidge 1. Lance-Corporal 18 7. Lance-Corporal P. Banning l7l PRIVATES' COMPETITION. 1. Bugler J. T. Jolley 2. Private E. Richaroison 26.. CLoanrpc 20 3. Private C. Wood . 20 4. Private H. Watkins 5. Private W. S. Draper G. Private R. Wicks 7. Private J. Thornton 8. Bugler W. Mellor 9. Private la. Carrigan 10. Private J. Frangleton 11. Private J. Collins</p>
